{
  "job_id": "ingest-probe",
  "text": "So I just checked this patient. He is around 52 years old and he's been having fever and cough for about 3 days now. The cough is productive and he's also complaining about some chest discomfort and shortness of breath. He says he's been feeling pretty tired and his appetite has also reduced. He already has a history of hypertension and type 2 diabetes mellitus. Coming to his vitals, his temperature is around 101 degrees Fahrenheit. His blood pressure is 130 over 85, pulses around 92 beats per minute and respiratory rate is 22. His oxygen saturation is around 94% on room air. I'm thinking this possibly could be community acquired pneumonia. We can probably get a complete blood count, C-reactive protein, chest x-ray and maybe a sputum culture as well. Since he's diabetic, we'll also need to keep checking his blood glucose. For the fever, he's been advised paracetamol 650 milligrams and the doctor has also considered the amoxilin with clavulic acid. We'll keep monitoring his temperature and oxygen saturation. If his breathing gets worse or his oxygen level drops further, he'll need another assessment and we may have to consider oxygen therapy.",
